harry: FYI noticed a nasty dup-index problem in the new Next ISR starter. On high traffic the server ISR regeneration plus edge embed calls lead to multiple index persists for the same content  causing repeated expensive rebuilds. repo: https://git.company/oss/next-isr-llama-starter
zoe: oof. is this specific to ISR/regeneration windows or during cold starts?
harry: mostly when ISR background revalidate runs at the same time as client nav that triggers an embed; we saw two separate processes both decide to build+persist because persist is not idempotent. logs show concurrent persists and different trace ids.
ops-bot: deploy 2026-04-02T09:12:00Z event=regenerate.start url=/docs/faq deploy.id=deploy-9001
ops-bot: kv.put docs/faq/snap vsize=180kb trace=trace-1
ops-bot: kv.put docs/faq/snap vsize=180kb trace=trace-2
zoe: looks like a TOCTOU race. any auth retries mixed in? sometimes auth backoff can cause the first persist to fail and a retry to rebuild.
harry: yes we also saw intermittent auth refresh (401->200) during spikes. combined with naive retry, each process will re-run build-and-persist, not realizing another succeeded. snippet of the problematic persist call in starter:
```js
// naive persist
const idx = await LlamaIndex.buildFromDocs('docs', docs)
await idx.persist() // no idempotency => multiple writes
```
claire: mitigation: make persist idempotent or use an atomic compare-and-swap in KV. e.g. write a version key first, use KV's conditional put, or include checksum and upsert-if-missing. SDK should help here.
ethan: proposing starter change: have the build path attempt to create a "lock" key with TTL, run build only if lock acquired, otherwise wait & load. plus use a persist version header. example (starter sketch):
```js
// pseudo-idempotent persist
const version = await kv.get('docs/faq/version')
if (!version) {
  const gotLock = await kv.put('docs/faq/lock', process.pid, { nx: true, ttl: 30 })
  if (gotLock) {
    const idx = await LlamaIndex.buildFromDocs('docs', docs)
    await idx.persist({ meta: { checksum: sha256(idx.snapshot) } })
    await kv.put('docs/faq/version', idx.meta.checksum)
    await kv.del('docs/faq/lock')
  } else {
    // wait for version to appear and load
    await sleep(200)
  }
}
```
zoe: good pattern. we should include a lightweight helper in the starter sdk wrapper: `ensurePersisted(key, buildFn)` that does lock+cas and returns the persisted version to callers.
harry: also adding an edge-friendly load that checks `X-Index-Version` header so client embed calls can short-circuit if they already have the right snapshot. e.g., server sets header when ISR rebuild completes, client includes it in embed request.
claire: for DX, add a new e2e eval harness that simulates concurrent ISR regenerations + edge embed requests (N=3 parallel) and asserts only one persist trace id exists and others load the same version. Wire this test into CI quickplay for starters.
ethan: small SDK enhancement request: expose persist checksum and an optional `persist({ ifNotExists: true })` API that uses KV atomic ops under the hood. Opened SDK issue #4828 and linked it in the PR.
zoe: also add guidance in starter README: recommend lock pattern or server-only builds when using ISR on high-traffic pages, and show the `ensurePersisted` helper.
harry: I'll open a PR with: (1) ensurePersisted helper + example, (2) lock/CAS example in build path, (3) e2e harness for concurrent persists, (4) README section about ISR+auth backoff footgun, (5) add quick telemetry markers so CI can assert single persist per content. tagging @claire for review.
claire: thanks. label this as high-impact DX for starters. once merged we should backport the helper to other starters (edge/ssr templates). :white_check_mark:
